$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure E for the Preparation of Benzanilide Substrates: In a
scintillation vial equipped with a stir bar was combined the amine (0.15
mmol, 1.0 equiv) and the di-Boc protected acid coupling partner (0.10 g,
0.29 mmol, 2.0 equiv) in THF (0.50 mL, 0.30 M). EDCI hydrochloride (29
mg, 0.15 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was subsequently added. The reaction progress
was monitored by LC-MS. Complete conversion of the amine starting
material to product was observed after approximately 1h. The solvent was
removed under reduced pressure, and the crude residue was then dissolved
in a 1:1 mixture of TFA:CH2Cl2 (4.0 mL total). After 1 h, the solvent was
removed. Purification by reverse-phase column chromatography (gradient:
10% MeCN to 100% MeCN in H2O + 0.1% TFA) and subsequent lyophilization.
The products as TFA salts. Substrate 5a: The coupling of commercially
available benzylamine by procedure E. 5a in 86% yield. 1H-NMR (400 MHz,
CD3OD d-4): δ 7.35-7.20 (m, 5H), 4.47 (s, 2H), 3.21 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H),
2.34 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 1.88 (quin, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CD3OD): δ 174.86, 158.78, 139.92, 129.55, 128.55, 128.24, 44.15, 41.84,
33.24, 25.98. HRMS (For C12H19N4O, MH+): Calc’d 235.1559, found 235.1575.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Identification of Multiple Structurally Distinct, Nonpeptidic Small
Molecule Inhibitors of Protein Arginine Deiminase 3 Using a
Substrate-Based Fragment Method
