$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To the stirred solution of acid 7.1(1eq) in
dry DCM were added HBTU (1.2 eq) and DIEA (1.5 eq) at 0 oC. After 5 min
1.2 eq of amine 7.2 was added and the reaction mixture stirred for 1 h at
room temperature, monitor the reaction by TLC. After completion of
reaction quenched with aq. NaHCO3 and extracted the aqueous layer with
dichloromethane, dried over anhydrous sodium sulphate and concentrated in
vacuo. Purified by flash chromatography, obtained pure product 7.3.
2-((2R,3R,4R,5S)-3-allyl-5-(((S)-2,2-dimethyl-1,3-dioxolan-4-yl)methyl)-4-hydroxy
tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-N-((S)-1-(allyloxy)-3-phenylpropan-2-yl)acetaminde
(7.3a):
2-((2R,3R,4R,5S)-3-allyl-5-(((S)-2,2-dimethyl-1,3-dioxolan-4-yl)methyl)-4-hydroxy
tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-N-((2S,3R)-1-(allyloxy)-3-methylpentan-2-yl)acetamide
(7.3b): Purified by flash chromatography using 50% ethyl acetate in
hexane; Yield: 86%. Molecular Formula: C24H41NO6; Rf (50% ethyl
acetate/hexane): 0.2; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 0.85-0.88 (m, 6H),
1.03-1.11 (m, 1H), 1.35 (s, 3H), 1.41 (s, 3H), 1.45-1.50 (m, 1H),
1.60-1.68 (m, 1H), 1.69-1.77 (m, 1H), 1.84-1.88 (m, 1H), 1.94-1.98 (m,
1H), 2.17-2.27 (m, 1H), 2.34 (dd, J = 14.2, 6.6 Hz, 1H), 2.38-2.46 (m,
1H), 2.52 (dd, J = 15.0, 3.0 Hz, 1H), 3.37-3.47 (dd, J = 10.0, 4.0 Hz,
1H), 3.50-3.60 (m, 2H), 3.60-3.68 (t, J = 15.6, 1H), 3.76-3.82 (m, 1H),
3.88-4.02 (m, 4H), 4.11 (td, J = 8.0, 5.4, 5.4 Hz, 1H), 4.14-4.23 (m,
1H), 5.02-5.30 (m, 4H), 5.76-5.94 (m, 2H), 6.55 (d, J = 9.1 Hz, 1H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 11.3, 15.4, 25.3, 25.8, 26.8, 34.9, 35.6,
37.9, 42.0, 50.7, 52.6, 69.7, 69.8, 71.9, 73.7, 78.4, 80.4, 81.4, 109.3,
116.9, 117.1, 134.6, 135.5, 170.2; LRMS: (ES+) m/z = 462 (M+23).
